    "result_text": "The full build succeeds. The suite contains the one acceptance test class and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a computed `displayName` field to owner responses, formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\n**What I did:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema. Since the DTO is generated from this spec, the `OwnerDto` now carries the field. It's `readOnly` (response-only), so it isn't accepted or required as input.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto`, backed by a small single-purpose `displayName(Owner)` helper that formats `getLastName() + \", \" + getFirstName()`. DTO shaping belongs in the mapper, so the entity stays free of presentation logic, and the formatting lives in one reusable place.\n\nBecause the created owner is read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` (whose `RespondWithOwner` responder already maps through `OwnerMapper`), the field is populated everywhere owners are serialized without touching any endpoint YAML or function class. The acceptance test (`$.displayName` = `\"LastName, John\"`) and the full suite pass.",
